HST Office: no LibreOffice name left in the installed version file or the Linux splash window.

- version.ini/versionrc: ExtensionUpdateURL is empty instead of LibreOffice's extension update
  service. HST Office never checks extensions online (hst-extensions.patch makes the check a
  no-op), so nothing reads it; the file no longer names the other suite's server.
- Linux (X11) splash window: its title is "HST Office" instead of "LibreOffice", the name a
  task bar or window list shows while the office starts.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/desktop/unx/source/splashx.c
+++ b/desktop/unx/source/splashx.c
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@
 {
     Window root_win;
     XGCValues values;
-    const char* name = "LibreOffice";
+    const char* name = "HST Office";
     const char* icon = "icon"; // FIXME
     XSizeHints size_hints;
 
--- a/instsetoo_native/CustomTarget_setup.mk
+++ b/instsetoo_native/CustomTarget_setup.mk
@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@
 [Version]
 AllLanguages=$(if $(gb_WITH_LANG),$(gb_WITH_LANG),en-US)
 buildid=$(shell cd $(SRCDIR) && git log -1 --format=%H)
-ExtensionUpdateURL=https://updateexte.libreoffice.org/ExtensionUpdateService/check.Update
+ExtensionUpdateURL=
 UpdateChannel=$(if $(ENABLE_ONLINE_UPDATE_MAR),LOOnlineUpdater)
 ReferenceOOoMajorMinor=4.1
 UpdateID=$(PRODUCTNAME)_$(LIBO_VERSION_MAJOR)_en-US
